  "label": "A dark joke scene using a Husky puppy to imply a suicide attempt was stopped by a rope",
  "description": "The scene is composed of three panels featuring a Husky puppy in different contexts, with overlaid text forming a dark joke. The top panel shows the puppy lying on grass, posing the question 'what stopped a suicidal boy from jumping?'. The middle panel shows the puppy on a wooden deck at sunset, and the bottom panel shows the puppy yawning widely. The punchline 'the rope' is placed under the yawning puppy, implying the rope is what stopped the jump, playing on the double meaning of 'rope' as in hanging. The spatial arrangement is vertical, with each panel stacked, and the visual elements are connected by the meme's narrative structure.",
